/-
  Support module for .lean files generated by `clightgen -lean`.

  Generated files start with `import Clightdefs; open CC`, so this module exists
  to give them a stable name to import.  Everything they reference now lives in
  `CCLib` (imported below): identifiers, machine integers, floats, the
  `common/AST.v` layer, the C type syntax and its layout semantics, the operator
  semantics, and the Clight AST together with its operational semantics.

  Historically this file held the whole hand-written AST mirror; it was split out
  into `CCLib/*` as the semantics was built up, without changing any of the names
  the printers emit.
-/
import CCLib

namespace CC

/-! ## Identifiers, machine integers, floats, and the AST layer

    `Positive`/`Ident`/`identOfString`, `Integers.*`, `Floats.*` and the
    `common/AST.v` types (`ATyp`, `XType`, `Chunk`, `CallConv`, `Signature`,
    `ExtFun`, `InitData`, `GlobVar`, `GlobDef`) all come from `CCLib`, imported
    above.  Names are unchanged, so files emitted by `clightgen -lean` are
    unaffected. -/

/-! ## Ctypes and Cop

    The C type syntax (`Ty`, `Attr`, `Member`, `CompositeDef`, the `tint`/`tptr`
    short names, …) and the operator types (`Unop`, `Binop`) now come from
    `CCLib.Ctypes` / `CCLib.Cop`, together with their *semantics* (`sizeof`,
    `fieldOffset`, `accessMode`, `Cop.semBinaryOperation`, …).  Names are
    unchanged, so files emitted by `clightgen -lean` are unaffected. -/

/-! ## Clight syntax and semantics

    The Clight AST (`Expr`, `Stmt`, `Function`, `FunDef`, `Program`,
    `mkprogram`, `swhile`) and its operational semantics now live in
    `CCLib.Clight`, imported via `CCLib` above.  Names are unchanged, so files
    emitted by `clightgen -lean` are unaffected. -/

end CC
